Z||000011||Sage||11-10-2001||09:23 AM||||That front end on Redoctober's pic is a "Shogun" front end.  They make it for many different cars.  I took one made for a Dodge 3000GT and made it fit a Chevy Beretta.  (Was ALLOT of work! Had to cut it in half both directions and completely fabricate the top mounting edge and lengthen and reshape both wheel wells.)  I have pics if anyone would care to see them.<P>How much interest would there be in one available for the Fiero?  I have one here now that could be used, but I'm not going to make a mold to produce 3 parts!  That's a big part.  Big part=big mold.  Big mold=EXPENSIVE" mold!  If there were enough interest for future sales, I might consider it.  Just putting out feelers as I did look at it as a possibility when I was working on the one for the Beretta.  Held it up to the Fiero, and thought it looked pretty good.  Then saw this picture, and said, "Huh, somebody already did it!  I think it looks cool, but a little "generic" only because they make it for so many different cars.  <P>Anybody got any thoughts-opinions?<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000012||GodSend||11-10-2001||10:51 AM||||I would consider one for sure... ||||reg||1
Z||000013||TRiAD||11-10-2001||11:49 AM||||The one in that pic really looks Photoshopped to me. <P>I don't think anyone has beaten you to it, they're just thinking about it real hard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85-Sig-2.gif">              <BR><B><I><u><FONT COLOR="red">TRiAD Motorsports</FONT></u></B> \\\\ <B>triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> //// Michael ~ 85 GT 4sp</I>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Sage||11-10-2001||12:52 PM||||Triad:<P>Looks that way to me too.  I am just hesitant to go to the hassle and expense of molding it to the Fiero to make the plug, then making the mold, as you are talking about a good size monetary investment, not to mention the couple hundred hours of labor.  This also brings up questions of infringement.  The finished product would be an original piece, but for all practical purposes, would look just like the front ends on more than a few ricer cars.  It's a pretty front end, but do we want to rice our cars?  There is also a rear fascia, integrated rockers with a non functional scoop and a rear fascia that looks pretty smooth with some alterations.  <P>After the Beretta I did was done and pics put up on a Beretta site, there were at least 35 inquiries as to where this kit could be purchased.  As it is right now, it is a one of a kind as it is not offered for the Beretta from the manufacturer.  I was approached about making molds from that one, but people asking where they can get it is a long way from them paying for it.  I decided against it for several reasons, one of which was that it is not my design.  Granted, it is totally unique on the Beretta, as there are no others, but it looks just like many ricer cars out there, which to me constitutes following the crowd, which I try not to do unless the crowd is going where I'm headed!<P>I would have to have at least 15 confirmed orders to make this a worthwhile project.  Even with that, you are talking several months before production could commence.  Mainly because of my own schedule, but that's the situation as I see it.<P>GodSend:<P>If you really want this kit, an option would be to get exact dimensions of your car and compare it to cars that this kit is available for.  Then buy the one that is closest to yours and find a fiberglass shop that would consent to mold it to your car.  Would not be a cheap project unless you can do it yourself or know somebody that works for $2.00/hr..  It would definitely be unique though!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||3
