Z||000019||pureSKID||11-11-2001||12:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>from the sounds of it he is not looking for a full body kit he is looking to keep the fiero somewhat fiero looking but maybe different ground FX's, scoops, spoilers, wide body kits... it also doesnt sound like he wants to spend 3k on a kit.....<BR>Kyle</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is exactly it!  Every other car has oodles of body kits for $500-$1000 USD.  Like i mean ground effects (front,rear,sides) and maybe even a spoiler.<P>Not a replica kit to make it a non-fiero for the cost of the whole car!.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Pontiaddict||11-11-2001||01:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>Having done a lot of photoshop car mods myself and for other people, I can easily recognize telltale signs of an edited pic. there are 3 ones easy to spot right away..<P>bonus points for wheoever sees all 3.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>4 actually...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>1 The edited parts are kind of blurry<BR>2 the shading/ highlights are wrong<BR>3 the nose doesn't have the reflection where it's been modified<P>Not that I could do any better.<P><BR>||||reg||1
