Z||000022||Luni420||11-11-2001||03:18 AM||||That red one is my friends car. I have driven that Fiero. We jokingly referred to that car as a 20 footer. It looks real tight at 20 feet but when you get closer you can tell the front end wasnt meant for the car. The bumper is only held on by 2 bolts. The guy who had the car before Jeremy totally messed up on it. Also due to the shape of the bumper, it hangs real low and scrapes on almost anything. It has potential to look real good though. And the car did look very unique and got lots of head turns. The spoiler is a Saleen spoiler made for a mustang and I thought it looked pretty good on it too. Currently that car is for sale if any of you are interested. He has all the parts for it and it runs. He also has a midnight blue stock Fiero front bumper for it. It has a real nice aftermarket suspension and brand new brakes with steel braided brake lines and some other stuff. Hes got mostly newer interior pieces for it as well. The thing is he got it for his wife and she was impatient for him to get it running right and went out and got a 91 MR2 Turbo. Also its the bumper off an MKII MR2 not MKIII. I just thought it was cool that someone was using those pictures. ||||reg||1
