Z||000024||Seanh||11-11-2001||02:02 PM||||Hmmm...that front end looks great. I might have to try somthing like that too. Anyone know how it was done or how dificult to do?<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly - 86 GT<BR>Back to my 3.1L...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Sage||11-11-2001||04:50 PM||||For any of you guys that are looking for body "mod kits", if you haven't already, you need to check out Ausfiero's site.  Or do a search on this forum for posts by Ausfiero or body kits.  He is developing a series of mods that can be "mixed and matched" that are very cool and let you use bolt on parts.  They will retain the original Fiero lines but let you individualize and update your car.  Very cool.  He does good fiberglass and is an excellent designer.  You can also check Jon (Pat) Kalsmiths' site Fibersmith for some of the items he offers.  <P>None of the major after market body kit makers offer much for our cars that I know of,other than complete body kits or something like the ZR1, which to me looks like a "little Vette",(why not just get a real Corvette?)<P>I believe that "shogun" kit that Ausfiero photoshopped  runs between $1,000 and $1,800 depending on what car you buy it for.  Shouldn't take a good fiberglass man more than 3 or 4 weeks to graft one to a Fiero that is close to the right size to start with.  Don't know what they would charge either, guess it depends on what their labor rate is and how long it takes them.  Realistically, I would guestimate around $3,000 for the entire project, including paint, strictly a guess unless you do the work yourself.<P>Just some suggestions.<P>Let's see what everybody comes up with!<P><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!:D||||reg||1
Z||000026||Luni420||11-11-2001||05:53 PM||||Fieroboy, Id tell you how it was done, but it wasnt really done. Like I said the guy just slapped it on and used 4 bolts to hold it on. It was a real crappy job. If you were able to make a support bracket underneath and have the bumper fiberglassed to the body or something like that, it would work. The bumper is off a MKII aftermarket body kit, just not sure which one. Im sure it would work. I bet Jeremy would sell this one to you if you wanted it. I have no idea how much hed want. His Email address if you are interested in the car or the bumper or whatever is triksterut@aol.com tell him Robb told you to mail him and ask a question.||||reg||1
